From 34f604a52accba8eb7bf7c56c2a2417735f6a6f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:57:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Zaptec Go 2 tile charging-active source; add EV
 max-current and Nibe effektvakt settings scaffolding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- backend/app.py: the 'Zaptec Go 2' dashboard tile's on/off state was
  sourced from binary_sensor.ev3_ev_battery_charge (the EV3's own kia_uvo
  charging flag), not the charger. Repointed to
  binary_sensor.ev_laddar_zaptec (the existing HA template helper already
  built on sensor.gpn049831_laddstatus == 'connected_charging') — same bug
  class as the discharge_inhibit fix from 2026-09-27.
- governor.ev_max_current_a (6-20A, settings_store/api.py/app.py): the
  ceiling peak_governor restores Zaptec's current toward was hard-coded;
  now configurable within the charger's own floor (6A) and Hakan's
  requested ceiling (20A).
- nibe.effektvakt_max_power_kw / effektvakt_governor_enabled + a new
  EFFEKTVAKT write-safety tier on NibeController (number.max_int_add_power_47212,
  number.fuse_47214): scaffolding for capping the F750's internal electric
  backup heater via its own 'effektvakt' power-guard function. Both
  registers confirmed live but 'unavailable' on Hakan's pump (effektvakt
  never turned on at its own panel) — read-only exposure added to
  core/nibe/live.py and NibeLiveCard.tsx for 'what is it set to now'.
  No automatic write path wired into the polling loop yet; that is a
  deliberate next step, not built in this pass.

Verified: pytest 71/71, tsc --noEmit clean, npm run build clean (2764
modules, unchanged), vitest 130/130.
